{
  "description": "Plateaus: e1RM within a rep range, progressing/stalled/regressing thresholds, new rep range, deload and return-from-break exclusions, per-hand, bodyweight reps, added load",
  "notes": [
    "Week ends 2026-03-07. Recent = 2026-01-25..2026-03-07 (42 days); baseline = 2025-11-01..2026-01-24 (84 days).",
    "Epley e1RM = load x (1 + reps/30), rounded: 200x5 = 233.3 -> 233; 210x5 = 245; 210x3 = 231; 200x3 = 220; 202x3 = 222.2 -> 222; 300x5 = 350; 280x5 = 326.7 -> 327; 60x10 = 80; 64x10 = 85.3 -> 85; 100x5 = 116.7 -> 117; 102x5 = 119; 25x5 = 29.2 -> 29; 35x5 = 40.8 -> 41.",
    "Change % = (recent - baseline) / baseline, one decimal: squat 12/233 = 5.2; bench 2/220 = 0.9; deadlift -23/350 = -6.6; curls 5/80 = 6.3; z press 2/117 = 1.7; pullups 2/10 = 20; weighted 12/29 = 41.4.",
    "Squat 2026-03-03 is named Deload: left out, so 4 recent sessions. Curls 2026-03-06 has stored phase Deload: left out, 3 recent. Z press 2026-01-28 is 58 days after 2025-12-01: left out, 3 recent.",
    "Baseline sessions sit in mid January so the only 21-day gap is the Z press one. Bench sessions run every 2 to 3 weeks from October (baseline: Nov 12, Dec 1, Dec 15, Jan 3, Jan 20). Bench record 231 on 2025-10-01; 157 days to 2026-03-07 = 22 weeks. Order: regressing, stalled, progressing, new rep range, not enough data; then by name."
  ],
